  "adaptations": {
    "chat": "Adapted to starter app accounts and one plain HTTP client through the platform module door; no SDK. Source hashes identify the published registry files before adaptation; executable code lives in lib/assistant and app. Replies stream from llm.chat; a model-drafted email becomes an approval request and is never sent from chat.",
    "memory": "Adapted to starter app accounts and one plain HTTP client through the platform module door; no SDK. Source hashes identify the published registry files before adaptation; executable code lives in lib/assistant and app. Scope is the project and the signed-in account, set on the server. Shared organisation memory moderation is left out.",
    "approvals": "Adapted to starter app accounts and one plain HTTP client through the platform module door; no SDK. Source hashes identify the published registry files before adaptation; executable code lives in lib/assistant and app. The approval inbox is kept in this app's Postgres; an approved email runs email.send with the request id as its idempotency key.",
    "wallet": "Adapted to starter app accounts and one plain HTTP client through the platform module door; no SDK. Source hashes identify the published registry files before adaptation; executable code lives in lib/assistant and app. Owner-only balance and spend; top-up and customer billing are left out.",
    "activity": "Adapted to starter app accounts and one plain HTTP client through the platform module door; no SDK. Source hashes identify the published registry files before adaptation; executable code lives in lib/assistant and app. Owner-only recent activity, falling back to daily totals; webhook administration is left out.",
    "theme": "Adapted to starter app accounts and one plain HTTP client through the platform module door; no SDK. Source hashes identify the published registry files before adaptation; executable code lives in lib/assistant and app. Fonts come from bundled font packages; app/theme.css carries the styles."
  }
